to float64, preserve signed zero and\\\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:420:  floating-point bytes. The carrier is Jing-owned; upstream has no float64\\\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:424:  integral JavaScript Number inputs; callers must supply BigInt for exact\\\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:425:  integers or the float64 carrier for floating-point content.\\\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:593:producer obligation likewise carries forward, as *Encoding contract*\\\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:650:  `dao.jing/keyword`, `dao.jing/symbol`, and `dao.jing/float64`, including\\\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:654:- Integer versus integral float; signed zero; infinities and NaNs; integer\\\\ndocs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md:657:  as its exact float64 widening, distinct from float64 0.1; Node and Dart\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:14:- **2026-11-21 (r5 → r6 hybrid architecture & focused profile scope):** Eliminated guest-UAST host-leak workarounds and collapsed fragmented control subsystems into a **three-tier hybrid model** (aligned with Unison, Koka, and OCaml 5): (1) promoted representation-sensitive pure ops (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed IEEE-754 `yin.vm.float`) into `:pure` host primitives backed by `dao.jing.cbor` / `dao.host.*`, eliminating raw-double stack-frame hazards and guest-side $O(n \\\\\\\\log n)$ sorting; (2) unified `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, safepoint interrupt dispatch, and cold error/limit policy traps into one composable guest algebraic-effect layer (`yrt.effect`) over `%capture` with zero Jolt kernel expansion; (3) focused swappable preludes on **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` for existing code in those languages) plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), dropping unnecessary off-diagonal N×M symmetry (such as `:yang.clojure/py-v1`).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:15:- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, plus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, applied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed native entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE derivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, dependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind with exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) address-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked trailing forms, pins, and C1 behavior independently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled shadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) `yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:65:   - Lowering preserves source CST identity; compiled UAST roots under different preludes have distinct content addresses (or identical addresses when two descriptors emit identical UAST) linked by explicit provenance datoms carrying the §6.5 compilation derivation record (r8: frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor address, resolved runtime closure, input, output — reconciled by module symbol on every compilation, including a single lowerer revision paired with a conflicting runtime pin).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:78:- **Interpreter configuration is stream-resident data.** `yang.tao.md` §2.2 requires that \\\\\\\"the grammar, name environment, and elaborator configuration participate in interpretation\\\\\\\" and that \\\\\\\"an interpretation result must name both its input and the interpreter that produced it.\\\\\\\" The hardcoded `py/*`-style coupling in the current lowerers buried that configuration in host code; the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` and `:yang.prelude/profile` lift it into portable, content-addressed artifacts, and the compilation **derivation record** names the interpreter exactly: `(frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor address, resolved runtime closure, input address, output address)` — one record, consistent with `yang.antlr.md`'s compilation derivation contract; the resolver's *derivation* belongs in provenance while its *live cell* belongs to the task.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:82:Consequence: switching a frontend's default semantics is a *data re-pin* (revision selection in `yang.frontend`), carrying zero code change and zero content-address churn for unselected profiles.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:138:| **Tier 1: Native Host `:pure` Core** | Host module exports (`:pure`, effects `#{}`) in `data`, `integer`, `float`, `kind` | **All four hold:** (1) one universal mathematical/representational truth across all languages and all 4 hosts; (2) host-representation-sensitive (avoids `Float64`/`BigInt`/keyword/HAMT leaks); (3) total or status-returning without suspending control flow or calling guest closures; (4) hot-path value operation. | Exact big-int math, boxed IEEE-754 float math & formatting, `data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, code-point strings. |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:165:   - **`data/float64? [x]`:** Backed directly by existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?` (`src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:212`). Distinguishes float64 carriers from exact integers, booleans, and maps on all 4 hosts.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:167:     - Exact int × exact int: `integer/compare == 0`; float64 × float64: `false` if either is `NaN`, else IEEE numeric equality (`+0.0 == -0.0` is `true`, `NaN == NaN` is `false`); exact int × float64: **`false`** (`1 != 1.0`).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:171:   - **`data/admit-key? [k]`:** Recursive portable key/element predicate preventing host map/set collapse (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`). Returns `true` iff `k` (recursively across vectors, maps, and sets) contains only `nil`, booleans, exact integers, strings, and keywords/symbols whose `name` is free of `\\\\\\\"/\\\\\\\"` and not starting with `\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"` — **an absent namespace is admitted (r8): the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only, so an unqualified `:k` admits**. Returns `false` for any `float64?` (at any nesting depth), ambiguous identifiers, seqs/lists, closures/continuations, or `:cell-ref` handles. **Integer-carrier normalization (r8):** distinct exact-integer carriers (`int64` vs boxed) normalize recursively on insertion AND lookup so equal integers hit the same entry.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:174:2. **Boxed IEEE-754 host module `yin.vm.float` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/float.cljc`, module name `'float`):** **Host-boundary conversion rule (r8):** boxed conversion and true-division results are exposed AT the host boundary (`integer/to-float` results and `true-div` quotients enter guest frames only as boxed `data/float64`); the zero-raw-double guarantee is scoped to profiles on the boxed path (the Clojure-family profiles). The frozen native ABI of the legacy preludes is unchanged.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:175:   - Operates exclusively on **boxed `data/float64`** inputs and outputs (plus exact integers where specified), returning either a boxed `data/float64`, a boolean/integer/string, or a pure status keyword (`:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `:yin.vm.float/underflow`, `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`, `:yin.vm.float/fractional-exp`, `:yin.vm.float/infinite-exp`).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:180:     - Division/floor/power: `floor` (total IEEE double floor), `floor-int` (exact integer for finite `|x| < 2^53`, else `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz remainder for finite `x >= 0, y > 0`), `floordiv-mod` (returns `[q r]` boxed pair or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, preserving `-0.0` quotient sign and `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` rounding correction), `fpow-half` (half-power squaring for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`), `fpow-base` (base squaring for `php`, preserving `1.1 ** 6` bit-exact oracle parity — see D7), `neg-pow` (`[x n pow-order]`, returns boxed `float64` or `:yin.vm.float/underflow`), `parts` (`[mantissa exp2]` exact integer pair).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:258:    :yang.prelude/revision \\\\\\\"2026-11-21.1\\\\\\\"\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:285:    :yang.prelude/revision \\\\\\\"2026-11-21.1\\\\\\\"\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:321:2. **Native language profiles (`py`, `js`, `php` — the Legacy compatibility track, built later):** Preserve full, faithful CPython/Node/PHP semantics for existing libraries and code that assumes them. The landed preludes already provide this at their current content addresses and remain the regression net (their oracle suites keep passing untouched). What defers is their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float — a separate legacy-modernization track, undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. Until then they run exactly as landed: frozen mechanisms, zero golden churn, selectable by pinning their revision.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:330:  2. Pure, closed literal-strategy emission (`:raw`, `:float64-raw`, `:tagged-map`, `:raw-or-call`).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:380:  :float   {:kind :float64-raw}      ;; vs {:kind :tagged-map, :tag :py/float}\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:486:- `:yang.frontend/id` names the frontend syntax + lowering implementation (e.g., `:yang.python/antlr`), and each profile gets an immutable `:yang.frontend/revision` (`\\\\\\\"py-v1\\\\\\\"` vs. `\\\\\\\"clojure-core-v1\\\\\\\"`).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:487:- `:yang.frontend/lowering-profile` pins the content address of the `:yang.semantics/descriptor` EDN artifact; `:yang.frontend/runtime-profile` pins the resolved `:yang.prelude/profile` manifest. **Descriptor/runtime reconciliation (r8):** where two lowerer revisions consume one descriptor, the pins are reconciled **by module symbol before lowering** — a conflicting pin fails closed. Dependency-first module installation belongs to linked composition (a verified dependency pin does not install its module in a cold task; first execution on a cold task is gated). The resolver's derivation is recorded in provenance; its live cell is task-owned.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:488:- Compilation provenance retains the exact derivation record (r8: frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:489:- **Default selector (r8):** the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[frontend-id revision]` pair, applied at the normal request entry; `yang.frontend/select`'s ID-only ambiguity resolves through that configuration. Gates: both revisions installed → ordinary request selects Clojure semantics; explicit legacy pin → native behavior preserved; in-flight request → original snapshot retained.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:503:| `1.5` | `{:py/float <float64>}` | `<float64>` (untagged Jing `data/float64` carrier) |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:522:     (if (data/float64? x) :float :other))\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:527:   - Exact ints promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (clj/rt-ctx) (integer/to-float-boxed i)))` — `integer/to-float-boxed` (r8) returns the boxed carrier at the host boundary so no raw host double crosses a guest frame.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:574:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:612:- **Zero bare integral float literals & zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** All float operations pass boxed `data/float64` through `yin.vm.float`, avoiding raw host doubles across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:646:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`; the bundled `yang.clojure` continuation family is a LEFT FOLD, not balanced — recorded as its own mode so the freeze is exact) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \\\\\\\"a/b\\\\\\\") != (keyword \\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"b\\\\\\\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:649:| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); the cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind gate — cleanup and context restoration, exactly once per activation — listed directly here; capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:657:1. **D10 — Default-profile policy & legacy-track deferral (`Settled — r7 Owner Directive`):** For the parameterized frontends, the **Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` first; ts/php to follow); the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist at their current content addresses with passing oracle suites), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to Track B until legacy demand justifies it. The clojure prelude family is built first. Consequence named in §6.1: capability refusals (classes, generators, typed `except`, `with`, kwargs) are the default experience for source written against native semantics; pinning the legacy revision is the escape hatch.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:666:   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:71:revision of `:yang/php`, its implementation named by the manifest's\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:72:revision and profile keys; the final naming at acceptance is the owner's.\\\\ndocs/design/yang.php.md:244:  the exact in