\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/generalize-params 2] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/prepare-argument-subst 6] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-app 4] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-args 3] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.typing/type-of-refdef 5] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.unparser/unregister-unparser! 1] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/map-with 3] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/vconcat 2] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/vcons 2] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", [latte-kernel.utils/zip 1] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"No passing direct fixture or named integration records this exact arity in both C lanes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:178:`F` not reducing to a Π is Reject (R-APP, `:not-a-function`). `A' ≢ A` is Reject (R-APP, `:argument-mismatch`).\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:191:**Rule R-CHECK.** `E; Γ ⊢ t : T` iff `E; Γ ⊢ t ⇒ T'` and `E; Γ ⊢ T' ≡ T`. The checker never guesses a type for `t` from `T`; there is no bidirectional refinement in v1. Failure of the conversion is Reject (R-CHECK, `:type-mismatch`) and reports both `T'` and `T` in weak head normal form.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:245:3. Compare heads: `sort` by L-4; `bvar` by index; `const` with the same name by L-4 on levels, then on mismatch unfold either side by C-4 if transparent and retry; `app` spines by head then pairwise arguments by C-9; `lam` and `pi` by domain then body under the extended context; `let` after zeta.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:270:**Rule O-4 (no host contribution).** Nothing the executing VM does, no primitive result, no effect and no continuation operation contributes a step to §4. If the kernel's execution encounters a host failure, the outcome is a harness failure, reported outside O-1, never a `Reject`.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:304:**Example D-c.** `theorem bad [] T (lam (sort zero) (lam (bvar 0) (bvar 1)))` into `·`: Reject (R-CHECK, `:type-mismatch`). The body returns `P`, of type `sort zero`, where `bvar 0`, of type `P`, is required.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:331:3. During a check the configuration is frozen (kernel plan §5). Any VM-level event that would alter it, a registry extension, a primitive redefinition or a store write outside the checker's own state, is a harness failure under O-4.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:356:Each fixture records the expected pair of outcomes. A mismatch with the recorded pair blocks; a match with Lean is neither required nor expected.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:377:`Accept` and `Reject` compare as above. A Yin `Unknown` never matches any oracle outcome and blocks a fixture that claims completed checking. A Lean resource exception is recorded as the oracle's `Unknown`, distinct from a Lean type error. A broken driver, translator or crashed process is a harness failure, not a negative fixture.\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:387:| F-5 | R-APP mismatch: `app t (sort (succ zero))` with `t` from §3.5 | Reject (R-APP) |\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.cic.spec.md:388:| F-6 | R-LET annotation mismatch | Reject (R-LET) |\\\\\\\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:18:| `semantic.scan-test` (then `semantic-register.scan-test`) C4 golden mismatch (JVM, Node) | slow tier at 355bd84b | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed 2026-10-14: the `[:c4 :py]` scanner golden regenerated mechanically after the other seat's linker relocation | P2 |\\\\\\\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:24:| `semantic/frame.cljc` (formerly :141; now ~:159) compares a captured frame's free-environment bindings with the task's free-env by host `=`; not NaN-reflexive on JS/Dart (a NaN-valued free binding in a captured/parked/waiting frame would be `:free-env-mismatch` there; same class as the 8f-3 NaN fix) | 8f-3 NaN ruling §5 | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed on branch `srvm-frame-nan` (Architect signed off; the commit is the one adding `bindings=` to frame.cljc): guarded slotwise content equality; JVM focused 116 tests / 1380 assertions and quick tier 4007 tests / 249662 assertions green, host-equality mutant 9 failures; [evidence](../collab/yin-vm/1792082835156-engineer-frame-nan.report.md) (Node/Dart lanes assigned to orchestrator) | P3 |\\\\\\\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:42:| `yin.vm.values` hashes a `Continuation`/`Closure` payload recursively (`values.cljc:99`, `(:continuation owner payload)`), so hashing a deep VM state overflows the JVM stack: `StackOverflowError` in `APersistentVector.hasheq`/`Murmur3.hashUnordered`, reaching `Continuation.hasheq` and `Closure.hasheq`. Surfaces as `yang.python.antlr.safepoint-test/recursion-error-test`, `linked-safepoint-test/linked-recursion-error-test` and two `e2e-test` recursion tests. Verified identical on shiva AND jupiter at 6d6b7e71 (19/141 + 1 error; 10/51 + 1 error; 42/714 + 2 failures), and present at the PARENT commit 3ab1c925 for safepoint-test; environment-sensitive (the same tests are green on the macOS dev machine at 19/144, 10/53, 42/714) `| bound the hash depth or hash a stable identity instead of the payload; needs \n... 307655 bytes omitted ...\n  :c1-digest \\\\\\\"302dee32f10d07ba31629c5d331badf9acf0bb5e886e98b15a42561aa4c24ee9\\\\\\\",\\\\n1505\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"f5b2dfd9d802b73edd9e71a78e90a3ad71be4bbbd2e2a61ac97c7a65d3e1d2e5\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1506\\\\t   {:case :heterogeneous-elements,\\\\n1507\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-4b25744274e0e43b20fd5faf2a922d717c6e8e5e951caec3604ef66218b6da85,\\\\n1508\\\\t    :applications 2,\\\\n1509\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"639469195e5ec9cdb63b2cc2c3b1e1e4f8336de1cfa1fc8e0a0b4f00fc4de4bd\\\\\\\",\\\\n1510\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"d1fb6b8990dbe8bca1eda6457ca5d22ff8b231107c535ff84b0115ad78aab7c6\\\\\\\",\\\\n1511\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"65a5de3d0810fbdec2cfb0b7dbbed80539ac7a9fa4d29c7642525b00c94af60d\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1512\\\\t   {:case :map-8,\\\\n1513\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-80d79cdfc99568571a3b45c8b58d88b140b3dd15d05f850d4d80fdb2ae5d769d,\\\\n1514\\\\t    :applications 9,\\\\n1515\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"c484175e9d11890148e7f120387caccd31c5c813864eca8d6c4978d199a25ae4\\\\\\\",\\\\n1516\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"00c69aee99f5830eff751d43871f6d590c1e99f20a32fe9250bd5706a0b37dcd\\\\\\\",\\\\n1517\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"6737012f112b2910f4bab85227a1222961679c209d18c55773a873980523b809\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1518\\\\t   {:case :set-8,\\\\n1519\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-7d04c498769369de939bf9b257f6b7335b3fb59e470778acd324e8f11784f061,\\\\n1520\\\\t    :applications 9,\\\\n1521\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"00297b53f66b4389c8ba832a7371f73520dfee2b8bde3646d90f451bd59feedf\\\\\\\",\\\\n1522\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"8b533b540a5b5b87ca03ff1edacd7122ce373df1cb0237135eb062c8af769770\\\\\\\",\\\\n1523\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"761bcf4caef42998bea643c2445d74f40f9c4f2f4c68ba6e515adfc8780a331b\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1524\\\\t   {:case :map-9,\\\\n1525\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-b459ddc89bcedbea983ebd2f518cad8375e6684151cb95387977d97064a53e02,\\\\n1526\\\\t    :applications 10,\\\\n1527\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"9a2a622cb6ef3469fde420cb9f388a24a7c2f021e14b8aeb1f080ef40fbbf348\\\\\\\",\\\\n1528\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"3f958fad25e72ed2024c6f24d4e006c1e58490663fc1f63e967b6fa238259c9b\\\\\\\",\\\\n1529\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"abac6cef64dd5dd7eb7e7b14e5788e73f2c8785f21c772072dc24877d8cc7e9f\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1530\\\\t   {:case :set-9,\\\\n1531\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-77324b2a95b9065a13380499b3b3f98353c3f1abaa2edf15cdb78026627e444d,\\\\n1532\\\\t    :applications 10,\\\\n1533\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"b42c2fd79a9ba8bd5706d651942b7b0a12d881c1494ed9082db9e005f434c823\\\\\\\",\\\\n1534\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"a91734d00cdbb3754071b7507ea5f5c95578154bc5f0cd9963db928198e3e164\\\\\\\",\\\\n1535\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"796d5717fad5b4f5be79e602ba0421480b0544e6522b1c019530b1e3c2852330\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1536\\\\t   {:case :map-16,\\\\n1537\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-84d925c00a8849dda46f5e9e528a60fed9362272af386915503febaf1edf9f47,\\\\n1538\\\\t    :applications 17,\\\\n1539\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"9d65bf12420716dfe4efedf656dac18f56af5b77fe4f512227c84589bfc1e0bd\\\\\\\",\\\\n1540\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"a12317be5d1c0f3e30e34e69c50c45c74efad0d60121706f7216f30d7c76a68f\\\\\\\",\\\\n1541\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"0cd72212d241c5a9d0b9bf796360d09e91bbf98fa3e3cf5aa0a2ce95f93a3440\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1542\\\\t   {:case :set-16,\\\\n1543\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-88c6a294f1e93c458d0c8b4b1e87dae7a44ff6c4479d2170af0fefcce670fec6,\\\\n1544\\\\t    :applications 17,\\\\n1545\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"91ccbddf0aa3310fdeba4520c159862badc47a6eb6315d513927c2f6b24e7d05\\\\\\\",\\\\n1546\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"54f39fe742cea6d93fab4d0e65e01d03e2b09517883d5d93e656f6ab890a7f63\\\\\\\",\\\\n1547\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"ef8c21b6f818383bd097d2d71a6ae85bc3c7f474b5cd733dd4aff169851fa97a\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1548\\\\t   {:case :map-32,\\\\n1549\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-b28f6cff1f295481b3ccd747acba0226e9a959f9d46a125f493faca96b979f12,\\\\n1550\\\\t    :applications 33,\\\\n1551\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"7ff031c2af1499aab281b0c1c48114e08d5643e9c5e47f04428a9ba7b66dfb7b\\\\\\\",\\\\n1552\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"396f336dfe0c7090b516800e4b14aa9b3db1ec01667b2b620098b5d39997a835\\\\\\\",\\\\n1553\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"ff00f6160a89a6dbac3d14134b3b92c407b8426ab8df746d7d6a2e7d172121f3\\\\\\\"}\\\\n1554\\\\t   {:case :set-32,\\\\n1555\\\\t    :root :segment/blake3-7dcea56d08b933e831ba943dc3359a30f9d56a7a7f85d09d192c3e0064911e71,\\\\n1556\\\\t    :applications 33,\\\\n1557\\\\t    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"f0ebb492a0d79846a13372fd2c9b7e4d7f4aded9b09c7836862c788c1dbcfab9\\\\\\\",\\\\n1558\\\\t    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"1e7173ae4842925197101f4d2309f69afe3d908aa6cc9f168d9ef21409d794f7\\\\\\\",\\\\n1559\\\\t    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"17d6153febc822c195d8ad62eb52c9102f6246ff60476aadf9377dbdd4fa01d3\\\\\\\"}])\\\\n1560\\\\t\\\\n1561\\\\t\\\\n1562\\\\t(deftest corpus-cross-host-reference-test\\\\n1563\\\\t  \\\\\\\"B3: every host compiles the broader corpus's canonical constructions to\\\\n1564\\\\t   the SAME recorded reference -- root, full C1/key vectors and per-format\\\\n1565\\\\t   provenance -- so corpus equality is a cross-host replay gate, not a\\\\n1566\\\\t   within-host property. The permutation/representation checks above stay\\\\n1567\\\\t   as additional properties.\\\\\\\"\\\\n1568\\\\t  (let [actual (into {}\\\\n1569\\\\t                     (map (fn [[case snapshot]] [case (dissoc snapshot :case)]))\\\\n1570\\\\t                     (concat\\\\n1571\\\\t                       (map (fn [[label entries]]\\\\n1572\\\\t                              [(keyword (name label))\\\\n1573\\\\t                               (compile-snapshot (build-map :array-map entries))])\\\\n1574\\\\t                            map-corpus)\\\\n1575\\\\t                       (map (fn [[label elements]]\\\\n1576\\\\t                              [(keyword (name label))\\\\n1577\\\\t                               (compile-snapshot (build-set :vec-set elements))])\\\\n1578\\\\t                            set-corpus)\\\\n1579\\\\t                       (mapcat (fn [n]\\\\n1580\\\\t                                 [[(keyword (str \\\\\\\"map-\\\\\\\" n))\\\\n1581\\\\t                                   (compile-snapshot (build-map :array-map\\\\n1582\\\\t                                                                (sized-map-entries n)))]\\\\n1583\\\\t                                  [(keyword (str \\\\\\\"set-\\\\\\\" n))\\\\n1584\\\\t                                   (compile-snapshot (build-set :vec-set\\\\n1585\\\\t                                                                (sized-set-elements n)))]])\\\\n1586\\\\t                               map-corpus-sizes)))]\\\\n1587\\\\t    (is (= (count corpus-reference) (count actual) 18))\\\\n1588\\\\t    (doseq [{:keys [case] :as expected} corpus-reference]\\\\n1589\\\\t      (testing (str case)\\\\n1590\\\\t        (is (= expected (assoc (get actual case) :case case))\\\\n1591\\\\t            (str \\\\\\\"cross-host corpus divergence at \\\\\\\" case))))))\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"df48b667-24b3-446f-ae43-a093b49fe632\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-26T12:25:59.476Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-floatkind/test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"  \\\\\\\"test/resources/yang/clojure/constructed-collections-legacy-c1-1.cbor\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- read-fixture-bytes\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The fixture file's bytes on the host (the yin.repl.store-test raw\\\\n   content-log pattern: nio on the JVM, fs on Node, dart-io on Dart).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [path]\\\\n  #?(:cljd (.readAsBytesSync (dart-io/File. path))\\\\n     :clj (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes\\\\n            (.toPath (java.io.File. path)))\\\\n     :cljs (.readFileSync (js/require \\\\\\\"fs\\\\\\\") path)))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest legacy-fixture-custody-test\\\\n  \\\\\\\"B2 custody: the retained binary artifact at the fixture path and the\\\\n   portable base64 copy embedded in this file are provably ONE artifact --\\\\n   their bytes are equal on every host -- and the file's payload decodes,\\\\n   carries the recorded c1-1 root, and runs to the recorded old value\\\\n   without recompilation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (let [embedded (base64/decode legacy-c1-1-payload-b64)\\\\n        from-file (read-fixture-bytes legacy-fixture-path)]\\\\n    (is (= (bytes/length embedded) (bytes/length from-file) 5403)\\\\n        (str \\\\\\\"both custody copies are 5,403 bytes; file has \\\\\\\"\\\\n             (bytes/length from-file)))\\\\n    (is (bytes/equal? embedded from-file)\\\\n        \\\\\\\"the fixture file's bytes EQUAL the decoded embedded copy\\\\\\\")\\\\n    (let [payload (cbor/decode from-file)]\\\\n      (is (= \\\\\\\"c1-1\\\\\\\" (:manifest-revision payload)))\\\\n      (is (= (:root payload)\\\\n             (get-in payload [:rows (:root payload) 0])))\\\\n      (is (= {0 :b} (:old-value payload)))\\\\n      (let [vm (ast-walker/vm-load-rows (tu/create-vm base-opts)\\\\n                                        (select-keys payload [:root :rows])\\\\n                                        vm/ast-contract)]\\\\n        (is (= (:old-value payload) (vm/value (vm/run vm)))\\\\n            \\\\\\\"the file-loaded artifact executes to its old value\\\\\\\")))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest legacy-artifact-loads-and-runs-test\\\\n  \\\\\\\"RULING 4: a retained pre-fix artifact loads at its old address and\\\\n   executes without recompilation, keeping its old operand order and old\\\\n   behavior; the same source freshly compiled under c1-2 canonicalizes.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (let [payload (legacy-payload)\\\\n        rows (select-keys payload [:root :rows])\\\\n        program (list (list (quote fn) [(quote x)]\\\\n                            (insertion-map\\\\n                              [(list (quote -) (quote x) 1) :a\\\\n                               (list (quote -) 1 (quote x)) :b]))\\\\n                      1)\\\\n        recompiled (yang/compile program)]\\\\n    (testing \\\\\\\"the artifact is complete and self-consistent\\\\\\\"\\\\n      (is (= (:root payload) (get-in payload [:rows (:root payload) 0])))\\\\n      (is (= \\\\\\\"c1-1\\\\\\\" (:manifest-revision payload))))\\\\n    (testing \\\\\\\"the rows load through the walker loader and run unchanged\\\\\\\"\\\\n      (let [vm (ast-walker/vm-load-rows (tu/create-vm base-opts)\\\\n                                        rows vm/ast-contract)]\\\\n        (is (= (:old-value payload) (vm/value (vm/run vm)))\\\\n            \\\\\\\"old operand order stays old executable behavior\\\\\\\")))\\\\n    (testing \\\\\\\"the old order is not the new canonical order\\\\\\\"\\\\n      (is (pos? (count (get-in payload [:old-operand-roots]))))\\\\n      (is (not= (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode recompiled))\\\\n                (:root payload))\\\\n          \\\\\\\"recompiling the same source mints the canonicalized tree\\\\\\\"))\\\\n    (testing \\\\\\\"the fresh compilation canonicalizes and changes the winner\\\\\\\"\\\\n      (let [ctor (first (map-constructors recompiled))]\\\\n        (is (strictly-ascending? (pair-keys ctor)))\\\\n        (is (not= (child-roots ctor)\\\\n                  (vec (:old-operand-roots payload))))\\\\n        ;; both keys evaluate to 0; the canonically last pair wins now\\\\n        (is (= (:old-value payload) {0 :b}))\\\\n        (is (not= {0 :b} (:ast-walker (run-form program {}))))))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest token-admission-distinct-origins-test\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Admitting the same content under two tokens yields one root and two\\\\n   distinct origin sets and occurrence-key vectors (the cohort negative\\\\n   member rule).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (let [form {(list (quote tap) :k) (list (quote tap) :v)}\\\\n        a (project-batch (yang/compile form) \\\\\\\"order-a\\\\\\\")\\\\n        b (project-batch (yang/compile form) \\\\\\\"order-b\\\\\\\")\\\\n        origins (fn [batch]\\\\n                  (into #{} (comp (filter (fn [row] (= :yang/call-site (nth row 3))))\\\\n                                  (map first))\\\\n                        (:rows batch)))]\\\\n    (is (= (:root (:tree a)) (:root (:tree b))))\\\\n    (is (not= (origins a) (origins b)))\\\\n    (is (not= (digest-snapshot a) (digest-snapshot b)))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private corpus-reference\\\\n  \\\\\\\"B3: the recorded cross-host reference for the broader corpus -- one\\\\n   canonical construction per corpus case (forward insertion through\\\\n   the array-map/vec-set builders), JVM-recorded under the cc4 cohort's\\\\n   digest model: root, application count, the canonical-sorted C1\\\\n   marker relation, the sorted occurrence-key vector, and all three\\\\n   instruction formats' call-provenance. Every host compares against\\\\n   THIS bundle, not only against its own permutations.\\\\n   Recorded at fix/constructed-collection-order base 7e6d720c with the\\\\n   r3 repairs applied (seed-normalized generator, restored legacy\\\\n   fixture), JVM OpenJDK 21.0.2+13-58, Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [{:case :constant-keys-dynamic-values,\\\\n    :root :segment/blake3-b1a8a08e99b51094c309a63a67617c98f078d757852875c0de6fb719f171b1b9,\\\\n    :applications 3,\\\\n    :keys-digest \\\\\\\"f6d2381c78852b52bd2d441db0c187914aff65e49c185d3b07f87deb35c497c6\\\\\\\",\\\\n    :c1-digest \\\\\\\"226243b869f7e88628a99c945b8bf60c3e6a38e5d1ce27468b07ace27f172dbb\\\\\\\",\\\\n    :instruction-provenance-digest \\\\\\\"0c965650cc02bb7f26620af1fa1dcb0f3058e66039a4cb5cc1fea426626469e5\\\\\\\"}\\\\n   {:case :dynamic-keys,\\\\n    :root :segment/blake3-a76fae17e3afe1f0e5ad4a067250ec0cdf67ec5d934109771ae7dc1