"1.0\\\\\\\" must not print \\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\"). So custom rendering needed. Let me check dao.host.float API.\\\\n\\\\nActually — wait. Reconsider: `#?@(:cljs ...)` DisplayKey pattern exists. I'll write in yin.repl:\\\\n\\\\n```cljc\\\\n(deftype DisplayFloat [text]\\\\n  #?@(:cljd [cljd.core/IPrint (-print [_ sink] (.write sink text))]\\\\n      :cljs [IPrintWithWriter (-pr-writer [_ writer _opts] (-write writer text))]))\\\\n#?(:cljd nil :clj (defmethod print-method DisplayFloat [f ^java.io.Writer w] (.write w (.text ^DisplayFloat f))))\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nand text from a canonical float printer. For the printer — reuse `yin.vm.float`'s format via making format-raw public? It's `(defn- format-raw ...)`. I could export a `format` — the module has 'format export! `(get float-module 'format)` — `(data/float64 x)` → `((yin.vm.float/float-module 'format) x)` — public access through the module map. In yin.repl: `((get yin.vm.float/float-module 'format) x)`. Hmm yin.repl requires yin.vm.float? It doesn't currently. Add require. On JVM: input must be cbor/float64? — a Double IS float64? on JVM → format works → \\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\". So I can render BOTH carriers and Doubles canonically → cross-host identical REPL text! JVM Double display changes from \\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\"(pr) to \\\\\\\"1.0\\\\\\\"(format) — for typical values identical; for 1e-5 differs (\\\\\\\"1.0E-5\\\\\\\" → \\\\\\\"1e-05\\\\\\\"). Any existing test asserting JVM float REPL text with exponents? grep '\\\\\\\"1.5\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\|\\\\\\\"0.5\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\|E-5' in tests later. Risk manageable; cross-host text identity is worth it. Hmm, but python clojure profile (uses display-clojure-value, not format-value) — unaffected.\\\\n\\\\nHmm hmm. But wait — format-value is also used for `(print ...)` args → `(print 1.5)` on JVM prints \\\\\\\"1.5\\\\\\\" today → with canonical → \\\\\\\"1.5\\\\\\\" (same). And print of 1e-5 → \\\\\\\"1e-05\\\\\\\" instead of \\\\\\\"1.0E-5\\\\\\\". Existing tests? grep for E-5 / exponent expectations... Let me note it and check during GREEN.\\\\n\\\\nActually, let me keep it even tighter: render ONLY carriers (cbor/float64? that are not number? — on JVM Doubles are numbers and float64?...). `(cbor/float64? 1.0)` on JVM → true (instance Double). Can't distinguish \\\\\\\"a JVM Double that came from a carrier constructor\\\\\\\" from any Double — there's no distinction on JVM, by design. So either all Doubles render canonically or none. Cross-host REPL text equality demands canonical for all float64 content. DO IT for all float64? (carriers + Doubles). Python clojure profile e2e (JVM-only) unaffected (different display fn).\\\\n\\\\nOK. Now — the linked path & \\\\\\\"catalog route\\\\\\\". Let me check how catalog publication/preview works — `call-site-admissions` / pending-publication — compilation through catalog for module publication uses :derive. Not critical for gates; gates name \\\\\\\"standard REPL/catalog route\\\\\\\" = eval-input through frontends/create-state. Good.\\\\n\\\\nNext: understand the derivation/ast-index path that records compiled programs (yin.repl index) — uses source? `tokenize state' vm''` at finalize — reads the ledger. Skip.\\\\n\\\\nNow let me look at the remaining pieces I haven't read:\\\\n1. `compile-quote` in yang.clojure (for quoted data preservation).\\\\n2. `lower-unit` (linked path entry).\\\\n3. How `:env`/`:free-env` resolution works for `+` in plain compile (vm/primitives lookup at runtime).\\\\n4. stream_eval_test (extend per RULING 5 test list? \\\\\\\"as appropriate\\\\\\\").\\\\n5. callsite_test.\\\\n6. `u/lit` — uast literal constructor (for factory use).\\\\n\\\\nLet me read compile-quote + check u/lit.\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"b2174bc6103748b982e9031a\\\"}],\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"output_tokens\\\":0},\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"519cc353-4ebf-4ee9-a727-f6a51287dd1a\\\