MED\\\\n`clj-=` now loops over `(seq more)` and tests `(if xs …)` (`numeric.cljc:181-190`).\\\\nDirect + REPL source-path tests cover `(= 1 1 false)`/`(= 1 1 nil)`/`(= 1.0 1.0 false)`\\\\n→ false, and `clj-!=` negation (`(!= 1 1 false)` → true). Green on JVM/Node (and the\\\\nDart/Jolt direct-arity subset).\\\\n\\\\n### B-4 (discard sentinel collision) — CONFIRMED\\\\nThe `::discard` value sentinel is replaced by a three-element control/value tuple\\\\n(`[:value val end-i]` vs `[:discard nil end-i]`) threaded through `read-form-1`,\\\\n`read-form*`, `read-delimited`, `read-next-required`, `read-forms`. Guest\\\\n`:yang.clojure.reader/discard`, `false`, `nil`, `:discard`, and `[:discard nil 0]`\\\\nare all representable in top-level/collection/required-form positions; `#_`\\\\ndiscard still works (`#_:yang.clojure.reader/discard 1.0` → `[1.0]`). Green on JVM & Node.\\\\n\\\\n### B-5 (anon-fn capture avoidance) — CONFIRMED\\\\n`read-anon-fn` now emits a parse-local, unforgeable `FnArgRef` and a\\\\n`collect-used-syms` + `fresh-param-sym` pass producing capture-avoiding\\\\n`p<k>__<n>#` / `rest__<n>#` params (`reader.cljc:452-588`). The 4-vs-12\\\\ncounterexample (`(let [p__1 10] (#(+ p__1 %) 2))` → 12), the 40-vs-22 nesting,\\\\nrest params, `p1__1#`-style collisions, determinism (`semantic-root` equal across\\\\nreads/siblings), and `#(#{% %1})` duplicate detection are all asserted. Green.\\\\n\\\\n### B-6 (lexical compatibility + syntax-quote) — CONFIRMED\\\\n`'` removed from `macro-terminating?` (so `x'`, `foo'bar`, `a''`, `ns/x'`, `:k'`\\\\nread); `@x` → `(clojure.core/deref x)`; `#^` and `#<` restored; portable syntax-quote\\\\npreserves `numeric-carrier?` scalars, `~`/`~@`, deterministic `x#` auto-gensym, and\\\\nuser metadata. The 33-case differential corpus runs the reader against\\\\n`clojure.tools.reader`/`cljs.tools.reader` on non-float grammar and compares values\\\\nAND metadata (`mapv meta`). Green. (I confirmed the nested-discard `#_#_1 2 3` parity\\\\nis correct against Clojure's READ_EOF-propagating `#_` semantics, corroborated by the\\\\npre-existing `yin.repl-test` expectation `[\\\\\\\"(quote [#_#_% % %1])\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"['%1]\\\\\\\"]`.)\\\\n\\\\n### B-7 (pre-pause integral float) — CONFIRMED\\\\n`gate5-pre-pause-integral-float-across-continuation-and-snapshot` computes\\\\n`(+ 1.5 0.5) → 2.0`, `(* 2.5 2.0) → 5.0`, `(* -1.0 0.0) → -0.0` BEFORE the pause in\\\\nboth the VM store and the lexical frame, then verifies float64 kind / value /\\\\nIEEE-754 bits / canonical CBOR identity across direct pause/resume AND full UCF\\\\n`lift-task → cbor/encode → cbor/decode → lower-task → resume`. The original\\\\n`gate5-parked-float-result-crosses-the-round` is retained. Green on JVM & Node.\\\\n\\\\n### TDD authenticity — CONFIRMED\\\\n`red-jvm-b2-b7.log` / `red-node-b2-b7.log` (11:35–11:36) show 27 tests with the exact\\\\ncounterexamples failing (`#{false 1.0 2}`→`#{}`, `(= 1 1 false)`→true,\\\\n`:yang.clojure.reader/discard` dropped, `(let [p__1 10] (#(+ p__1 %) 2))`→4,\\\\n`x'`→EOF, `` ` ``→refusal): JVM 88 failures/14 errors, Node 88 failures/14 errors.\\\\n\\\\n### Clean full GREEN + regressions — CONFIRMED\\\\n- JVM 7-gates + PHP + corpus: 28/587 + 2/22, 0 failures.\\\\n- **JVM full regressions (single clean run, 12 namespaces incl. yang.clojure-test\\\\n  and yin.repl-test): 306 tests / 3,500 assertions / 0 failures, 0 errors** — this\\\\n  closes my r1 D-1 (the earlier stale `green-jvm-regressions.log`).\\\\n- Node 7-gates + PHP + corpus: 30/605, 0 failures; Node regressions 178/2137, 0\\\\n  failures; Node REPL re-check 67/335, 0 failures.\\\\n- Dart 69/69; Jolt float-kind 27/75/75, PHP 45/45, float 108/108, corpus 0/0;\\\\n  `yin.vm.data-test` 527/530 with the same 3 pre-existing Chez unpaired-surrogate\\\\n  errors (`:jolt/unimplemented dao.host.text/units->string`).\\\\n- kondo 0 errors / 5 warnings, all in untouched sections (no warnings in r1/r2\\\\n  edited files); the D-2 `clojure.string` warning is g